# Equipment Financing Page Standard

Use this guideline when creating or updating equipment type pages (e.g., excavators, bulldozers, forklifts). Reference: `equipment/excavators/index.html`.

---

## Page Structure (In Order)

1. **Hero Section** (`ef-hero`)
   - Full-width hero with background image (use `/assets/[equipment]-hero-bg.png` or generate if missing)
   - Blue gradient overlay matching industry/service pages
   - H1: "[Equipment] Financing: Equipment Loans, Leases & SBA Programs"
   - Subhead: 1–2 sentences on costs, approval speed, new/used
   - 4 bullet points (✓) with key benefits
   - CTAs: Primary (Apply) + Secondary (Back to Equipment)
   - Inline styles for hero (copy from excavators page)

2. **Trust Stats** (`trust-section`)
   - "At a Glance" with 6 stats: Typical range ($), Approval time, Terms, Down payment, Credit, Nationwide

3. **Intro with Image** (`ef-intro-with-img`)
   - H2: "Why [Equipment] Financing Makes Sense for [Industry]"
   - 2–3 paragraphs: equipment role, industry cash flow, why financing helps, resale value, tax benefits
   - CTA button
   - Image from `/assets/[equipment]-equipment.png`

4. **What Is [Equipment]?**
   - Define the equipment, common uses, industries that use it
   - 1–2 paragraphs

5. **Why [Equipment] Financing Is Different**
   - Lender perspective: resale value, asset-backed, industry-specific underwriting
   - Link to relevant industry page and equipment articles

6. **Financing Options** (`benefits-grid ef-equipment-cards`)
   - 3 cards: Equipment Loans, Equipment Leasing, SBA Loans
   - Each with image, H3, 1–2 paragraph description, internal link
   - Brief working capital vs equipment note
   - CTA

7. **How Much Does [Equipment] Cost?** (`ef-industry-row`)
   - New pricing (ranges by size)
   - Used pricing (30–50% less, age limits)
   - Factors: brand, attachments, regional demand
   - Link to calculator and used-equipment article

8. **Rates and Monthly Payments**
   - Typical rate range (6–15%)
   - Example calculations (e.g., $150K at 8%/60 mo ≈ $3K/mo)
   - Links to rates article, calculator, down-payment article

9. **Requirements Table**
   - Credit score, Down payment, Time in business, Revenue, Equipment quote
   - Follow with 4 short paragraphs expanding each requirement
   - Link to credit-score and lender-approval articles

10. **What to Have Ready Before You Apply**
    - Bullet checklist: bank statements, tax returns, P&L, equipment quote, formation docs, business info
    - 1 paragraph on having docs ready

11. **When to Apply**
    - Best timing, early application, avoid last-minute rush
    - 1–2 paragraphs

12. **Tips to Get Approved**
    - 5–6 bullets: credit, documentation, used equipment, down payment, resale value, broker

13. **Common Mistakes to Avoid**
    - 5 bullets: quote, financials, rate focus, timing, used equipment
    - Link to red-flags article

14. **Why Businesses Finance Rather Than Pay Cash**
    - Cash flow, tax benefits, reserves
    - 1–2 paragraphs

15. **Process Steps** (`steps-grid`)
    - 4 steps: Get Quote & Apply, Match With Lenders, Review & Approve, Funding & Closing
    - CTA

16. **Related Equipment** (`benefits-grid`)
    - 4 cards linking to similar equipment pages
    - Buttons: Browse All Equipment, Apply Now

17. **FAQ** (`faq-list`)
    - 6–8 questions: used equipment, credit score, approval time, lease vs buy, startups, documents, monthly payments
    - Each with 1–2 sentence answer + internal link where relevant

18. **More Resources**
    - Bullet list of 5–6 links to equipment-financing articles and equipment.html

19. **Final CTA** (`services-cta`)
    - H3, 1 sentence, Apply button

---

## Content & SEO Requirements

- **Word count:** 2,500–3,000+ words (body content)
- **Tone:** Professional, helpful, clear. Speak to contractors/business owners.
- **Internal links:** Include 12–18 links to: equipment-financing.html, match.html, calculator.html, equipment.html, relevant industry page, and equipment-financing/articles/* (credit, rates, used equipment, loan vs lease, down payment, red flags, approval speed, what lenders look at)
- **Keywords:** Use equipment name, "equipment financing," "equipment loans," "equipment leases," cost ranges, approval time, credit requirements naturally throughout

## Meta & Schema

- **Meta description:** 150–160 chars, include equipment name, cost range, approval time, credit, CTA
- **Title:** "[Equipment] Financing Guide: Equipment Loans, Leases, SBA | Costs & Rates | Axiant Partners"
- **Schema:** BreadcrumbList, FinancialService, FAQPage (all FAQ Q&As), Article, HowTo (4 steps)

## CSS Classes

- Form container: `form-container equipment-financing-content construction-content ef-content`
- Hero: `ef-hero`, `ef-hero-copy`, `ef-subhead`, `ef-hero-bullets`, `ef-hero-ctas`
- Page wrap: `ef-page-wrap`, `ef-content`
- Sections: `about-section`, `trust-section`, `ef-intro-with-img`, `ef-industry-row`
- Cards: `benefit-card ef-card-with-img`, `ef-card-img`
- Table: `financing-options-chart`
- Steps: `steps-grid`, `step-card`, `step-number`
- FAQ: `faq-list`, `faq-item`

